{"name":"Partha Bhoumik","details":{"designation":"Lecturer","email":"partha.bhoumik@bracu.ac.bd","address":"CSE Department 4th floor, Room No # 4M108, Brac University, Kha 224 Bir Uttam Rafiqul Islam Avenue, Merul Badda, Dhaka, Bangladesh","roles":["Supervisor","Co-supervisor"],"levels":["Undergraduate"],"types":["Thesis","Project","Internship"],"research_interests":["I have a keen interest in cyber security and blockchain technologies. I find the idea of securing digital systems and protecting sensitive data fascinating. Additionally","the concept of blockchain and its potential to revolutionize various industries captivates me. Moreover","I am particularly intrigued by the field of Threat Intelligence","as it involves gathering and analyzing information to proactively identify and mitigate cyber security risks. I am actively exploring the domain of image processing and computer vision","particularly in the context of security and threat detection . I am interested in how visual data can be analyzed using machine learning and deep learning techniques to support applications such as surveillance analytics","anomaly detection","biometric systems","and digital image forensics. In addition to my interests in cybersecurity and blockchain technologies","I am also deeply interested in software engineering . I am motivated to create software systems that are secure","reliable and meet the highest standards of quality and performance."]}},
